The dashed curve is $y=\arctan x$ and the solid curve is its image after one transformation.
Which transformation has been applied?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.7cm, y=0.75cm]
\draw[->] (-4.6,0) -- (4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.8) -- (0,4.0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed] (-4.4,3.1416) -- (4.4,3.1416);
\draw[dashed] (-4.4,-3.1416) -- (4.4,-3.1416);
\draw[dashed] (-4.4,1.5708) -- (4.4,1.5708);
\draw[dashed] (-4.4,-1.5708) -- (4.4,-1.5708);
\draw[dashed,domain=-4.4:4.4,samples=100,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{rad(atan(\x))});
\draw[thick,<->,domain=-4.4:4.4,samples=100,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2*rad(atan(\x))});
\node[font=\small,above] at (-3.0,3.1416) {$y=\pi$};
\node[font=\small,below] at (-3.0,-3.1416) {$y=-\pi$};
\node[font=\small,above] at (2.6,1.5708) {$y=\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\node[font=\small,below] at (2.6,-1.5708) {$y=-\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph of $y=\arcsin x$ is shown.
It is reflected in the $x$-axis and then translated $\frac{\pi}{2}$ units up.
What is the equation of the image?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.4]
\draw[->] (-1.8,0) -- (1.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.0) -- (0,2.3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=-1.5708:1.5708,samples=80,smooth,variable=\t] plot ({sin(deg(\t))},{\t});
\fill (1,1.5708) circle (1.6pt);
\fill (-1,-1.5708) circle (1.6pt);
\draw (1,0.07) -- (1,-0.07);
\node[below,font=\small] at (1,-0.07) {$1$};
\draw (-1,0.07) -- (-1,-0.07);
\node[below,font=\small] at (-1,-0.07) {$-1$};
\draw (0.07,1.5708) -- (-0.07,1.5708);
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,1.5708) {$\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\draw (0.07,-1.5708) -- (-0.07,-1.5708);
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,-1.5708) {$-\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\node[font=\small] at (-0.95,1.95) {$y=\arcsin x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The curve shown is a transformation of $y=\arccos x$.
What is its equation?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.25]
\draw[->] (-1.9,0) -- (1.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.9) -- (0,0.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=0:3.1416,samples=80,smooth,variable=\t] plot ({cos(deg(\t))},{-\t});
\fill (1,0) circle (2pt);
\fill (-1,-3.1416) circle (2pt);
\draw (1,0.07) -- (1,-0.07);
\node[above,font=\small] at (1,0.09) {$1$};
\draw (-1,0.07) -- (-1,-0.07);
\node[above,font=\small] at (-1,0.09) {$-1$};
\draw (0.09,-1.5708) -- (-0.09,-1.5708);
\node[right,font=\small] at (0.12,-1.5708) {$-\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\draw (0.09,-3.1416) -- (-0.09,-3.1416);
\node[right,font=\small] at (0.12,-3.1416) {$-\pi$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
